course: dictionary
lesson: 4813
title: Hunchback: a word to use with care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hunchback is a back with a big hump or curve. It can come from a medical condition called kyphosis. «Slouching does not give children a hunchback (a back bent into a hump).»
explain: Hunchback is an old-fashioned word, and it can hurt people. Today it is kinder to say a person with a curved spine. You will still meet the word in old stories and films.
explain: Read the context to find the meaning. The words «back bent into a hump» tell you what a hunchback looks like, and the sentence is about posture, which is how you sit and stand.
fact: A hunchback is a back with a big hump or curve.
fact: The hump can come from a medical condition called kyphosis.
fact: Hunchback is old-fashioned and can be hurtful, so use it with care.
fact: Today it is kinder to say a person with a curved spine.
fact: The Hunchback of Notre-Dame is a famous novel by Victor Hugo about Quasimodo.
exercise: «Slouching does not give children a hunchback.» What is a hunchback? | A kind of bird | A straight, strong spine | A sore knee from running | *A back with a big hump or curve
exercise: Today, which is the kinder way to describe someone with a curved back? | A hunchback in an old story | A bent old tree | A humpback whale | *A person with a curved spine
exercise: Who wrote The Hunchback of Notre-Dame? | *Victor Hugo | Charles Dickens | Lewis Carroll | Roald Dahl
test: «Sitting badly for hours can cause aches, but moving about and strong muscles matter more.» What does this tell you about posture? | *How you sit and stand affects your back | Strong muscles make you taller | Aches always mean a hunchback | Posture only matters for dancers
test: Which word is old-fashioned and can hurt people? | Posture | Muscle | *Hunchback | Spine
exam: Which name for the whale with a big hump is correct? | Hunchback whale | *Humpback whale | Spine whale | Hump whale
